course: dictionary
lesson: 11842
title: A word from old poems
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are old. You will not hear them in playground talk, but you will find them in old poems and old children's books. Blithesome is one of these words, and you can work out much of its meaning by looking at its parts.
explain: Blithe means cheerful, and -some means full of, as in handsome or lonesome. Put them together and blithesome means full of cheer. «The blithesome puppy bounced across the garden, wagging its tail.» The puppy is happy and full of fun, so blithesome fits.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The cheerful puppy bounced across the garden, wagging its tail.» It still makes sense, so you have understood the word. Good readers do this every time.
fact: Blithesome is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a person, a mood or a day.
fact: Blithesome means cheerful, merry and light-hearted.
fact: Blithesome can also mean carefree, not worried about anything.
fact: Blithesome is old-fashioned, so you will mostly meet it in poems and old children's books.
fact: The word is built from «blithe» (cheerful) and «-some» (full of), like «handsome» and «lonesome».
exercise: «The blithesome children skipped home from school, singing.» What does blithesome mean? | *Cheerful and merry | Lost in the woods | Very hungry | Tired and cross
exercise: The word blithesome is made of blithe and -some. What does -some mean in this word? | Before | Not at all | Under | *Full of
exercise: Which feeling best fits the word blithesome? | Angry and loud | Sleepy and cold | *Happy and carefree | Scared of the dark
test: «Grandma was blithesome all day, humming as she baked.» What does blithesome mean here? | Very sleepy | Lost and lonely | *Cheerful and merry | Cross and grumpy
test: Why is blithesome called an old-fashioned word? | It comes from a language of the sea | It is a brand new slang word | *You meet it mostly in old poems and books, not everyday talk | It means exactly the same as sad
exam: Which sentence uses blithesome correctly? | *«The blithesome singer skipped onto the stage, grinning.» | «The blithesome puddle was cold and dark, and it made her cry.» | «He felt blithesome after he lost his favourite toy and cried all day.»
